   "html_text": "Yet Henry adds in this regard that those who have not been able to distinguish among the many meanings of being (as instead Aristotle correctly did), and have rather understood being as one genus (as Plato did), held that the name ‘being’ referred to a single and common concept. Univocity is therefore, according to Henry, a mistake, the origin of which lies in the indeterminacy of the concept of being which is first known by the intellect. In actual fact, as mentioned above, indeterminacy is two",
